iate.","Move people away from live traffic when possible."]},{"heading":"Safe application","body":"Use hazard warnings where appropriate.","bullets":["Move people away from live traffic when possible.","Use safe warning methods without walking into danger."]},{"heading":"Test tip","body":"Visibility matters after an incident.","bullets":["Visibility matters after an incident.","Never trade your own safety for a warning device."]}],"key_points":["Use hazard warnings where appropriate.","Move people away from live traffic when possible.","Use safe warning methods without walking into danger."],"exam_tips":["Visibility matters after an incident.","Never trade your own safety for a warning device."],"tags":["incidents and first response","warning","warning other traffic"]},{"id":"gb_052","category":"Incidents and first response","module":"Reporting","order":4,"title":"Information and reporting","minutes":14,"summary":"Drivers involved in incidents may have duties to exchange details or report what happened.","sections":[{"heading":"Core idea","body":"Drivers involved in incidents may have duties to exchange details or report what happened.","bullets":["Remain calm and record information safely.","Do not argue at the roadside."]},{"heading":"Safe application","body":"Remain calm and record information safely.","bullets":["Do not argue at the roadside.","Follow the legal reporting requirements that apply to the situation."]},{"heading":"Test tip","body":"Safety first, paperwork second.","bullets":["Safety first, paperwork second.","Accurate details are better than blame."]}],"key_points":["Remain calm and record information safely.","Do not argue at the roadside.","Follow the legal reporting requirements that apply to the situation."],"exam_tips":["Safety first, paperwork second.","Accurate details are better than blame."],"tags":["incidents and first response","reporting","information and reporting"]}]'::jsonb, 'TeoriX original study content v1.2', true, now())
